{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares","id":1555159,"title":"Entering and altering Chimares","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-11-06T04:08:59-08:00","id":1555159,"title":"Entering and altering Chimares","content":"I'm interested in whether STs have introduced house rules for their players to interact with dreams of individuals. So far, I have resolved questions narratively when the situation happened but it looks like I'm going to need some crunch because it is going to be 'a thing' in an ongoing Chronicle.<br /> I have a mixed group, and so far the Oneiromancer has handled most dream interactions (they have the right kit, after all), but I would like for the Fera characters to have a more active role as well without disadvantaging the Sorcerer.<br /> <br /> The books say that to enter the Dream Zone, Fera need to fall asleep in the Penumbra, and I have used that simple mechanic to let them enter a Chimare if the sleeping/dreaming individual is nearby, with a bit of an Inception flavor. However, I feel there should be some natural barrier similar to the Gauntlet that needs to be overcome, especially if the Chimare is something the dreamer crafted via lucid dreaming or a proper Demesne. Do you have some additional conditions for entering/exiting Chimares in your games, or can the characters simply 'walk in'?<br /> <br /> Rite of Dreamtime (Level Two) allows creation and manipulation of your own Chimare (likely aimed at creating a Demesne or Den Realm), and I could see that Rite to be adapted for altering the Chimare of others. The price for changing things inside is a rather steep Gnosis cost though, and it is probably easier to manipulate a dream through interaction with the dreamer Inception style. If you had dream quests like that in your Chronicles, I would be interested in hearing about how you handled dream manipulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T04:35:16-08:00","id":1555160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares#post1555159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I<br /> The books say that to enter the Dream Zone, Fera need to fall asleep in the Penumbra, and I have used that simple mechanic to let them enter a Chimare if the sleeping/dreaming individual is nearby, with a bit of an Inception flavor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it helps, but they not enter physically<br /> &quot;Her slumbering mind reaches through the mist of thought and into Dream itself.&quot; only their mind enter, body left behind sleeping in the Penumbra - witch is if no one guards their body is quite dangeros if not borderline suicidal<br /> I think this is quite a drawback and dangerous enough - so I let them sleep and suffer the consequences so to speak<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T10:55:37-08:00","id":1555165,"title":"","content":"I've always wanted to make dreams and dream travel an important part of my chronicles so I have researched this extensively and come up with my own interpretation of it. However, my players are generally uninterested so I've never used them in play so I don't know how well everything works. But this is what I use.<br /> <br /> Chimares are simply domains in the Penumbra. They are linked to the Dream Zone, but the Dream Zone is separate.<br /> <br /> Chimares are just individualized dream domains of a single dreamer. The early editions stated EVERY dream generates its own Chimare, but later editions seemed to walk that back and implied only the most powerful dreams generate Chimares. So pick whatever works best for you and your gaming group. Garou in the Penumbra may enter any Chimare they wish simply by choosing to enter them just like they do any other domain. When Garou are in a Chimare, it's just like any other umbral domain - they can encounter spirits, emanations, and other creatures (like a Wraith who uses the Arcanoi Phantasm). And of course the dream self of the dreamer herself.<br /> <br /> Some STs do want some additional challenges when entering domains like certain dice rolls (usually involving Enigma because that is what is used to navigate the Umbra) or figuring out certain tasks or riddles. It's all up to how easy or hard you want to make it. I generally make it very easy to enter dream Chimares. Any challenges or dice rolls are what happens once they get inside and try to do something.<br /> <br /> The Galliard Gift Dreamspeak allows a Garou to enter someone's dream (a Chimare) although in this case the Garou does not need to be physically present in the Penumbra next to the Chimare to do so. Presumably when the Gift is succesfully activated, the Garou simply vanishes from their current location and appears directly into the Chimare. Although not stated in the Gift description, I assume that when the Garou wants to end it, they simply pop back out of the Chimare and return to where they originally vanished.<br /> <br /> Likewise the Galliard Gift Gift of Dreams allows Garou to craft a specific and potent dream for an individual. In essence, this creates a specific Chimare for that individual to inhabit.<br /> <br /> There are also what I call &quot;independent&quot; Chimares. These are semi-permanent domains that exist independently from dreamers. They are usually formed as a result of many dreamers over time at the same general area, or are a result of powerful dream spirit energy in a location. One example is described at the Sept of the Green when the Wyld aided by the caern totem created a Chimare at Turtle Pond in Central Park. People who sleep there have incredible, inspirational dreams.<br /> <br /> <br /> All Chimares connect to the Dream Zone. When the dreamer awakes, any Garou or other entity inside the Chimare, are cast out into the Dream Zone or some sub-realm outside the Penumbra. If you want to directly travel from a Chimare to the Dream Zone you can, but I'd make it so that such Garou need to undergo a prolonged quest to go deeper and deeper into the subconscious before they can actually make it to the Dream Zone. It's usually much safer for Garou to travel directly to the Dream Zone via their own methods (sleeping in the Umbra, the Rite of Dreaming, or certain fetishes) than try to do that in someone's Chimare. Individual dreamers do sometimes enter the Dream Zone directly from their own Chimare, but those incidents tend to be fairly rare. Certain individual people can be more prone to experience such potent, deep dreams than others.<br /> <br /> Individual dreams link to the Dream Zone, but the Dream Zone is also where archetypal, lost, incomplete, or collective dreams reside. Generally if Garou want to explore these kind of dreams, or undergo Dreamquests to understand the meaning of important/persistent/prophetic/powerful dreams, then they'll ultimately need to go to the Dream Zone. The travel to the Dream Zone is when you can create more complications or require real spiritual quests.<br /> <br /> One thing I've done in my own chronicles is have a few of these persistent &quot;dreamrealms&quot; hidden in the Dream Zone described. I include them as a standard ongoing element that I use for the purposes of flavor text and plot hooks. They're inspired by the Dreamland stories of HP Lovecraft, Neil Gaiman's the Sandman, and other horror or fantasy stories that utilize some kind of common dream trope or setting. I have a remnant dream of the Summer Country when I want to emphasize positive aspects of the world or spiritual learnings. There's also a dream of the &quot;Table Rock&quot; where the Garou developed the first version of the Litany. I have something I call the &quot;Vale of Doom&quot; whenever an NPC has prophetic or predatory dreams that will build up to their own deaths. It's meant as a Wyrm influenced dreamrealm so the Garou PCs can undertake a quest to save the NPC's life. I have the &quot;Night School&quot; which provides insights into forbidden occult knowledge. It's another Wyrm influenced dreamrealm that tries to tempt and recruit people into Wyrm sorcery. There is the &quot;Blockula&quot; based on folklore about witches where servants of the Wyrm are able to gather in their witches' sabbaths and converse with other Wyrm witches. There's the fabled city of &quot;Syrannon&quot; which is very similar to Lovecraft's fabled dream cities, and mentioned as the goal for the Zolondondere in the Sorcerer sourcebooks. I add more such dreamrealms all the time as I get inspired or decide it is needed in the game either as a place to adventure, or as a recurring dream element that is common to some group (particularly Garou, but not exclusive to them). These kinds of recurring dreams are rare, but I found that players like them as when they appear it's a sign they can go on an interesting adventure or realize the dream have more than personal significance. They're good as omen (for dream interpretation rolls) or when someone has the Gift Sight from Beyond. I am for a mix of benevolent, benign, neutral, or hostile dreamrealms.<br /> <br /> I also have a very hostile Wyrm Nightmare dreamlord reside in the Dream Zone that is actively trying to invade Gaia's dream and corrupt reality. It's basically a counterpart to Chimera and the other unnamed Dreamlords of Earth. I built an entire faction around it. I've mentioned it chronicles, but haven't heavily utilized it in any chronicles yet. I'm waiting until a group actually wants to have Chimera as their pack totem. (Of course there are also various other Nightmare spirits, but those aren't necessarily anti-Gaian).<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200bThe Umbra sourcebooks talk about the Dream Zone, but not all sourcebooks are equal. The Revised Umbra in 2001 has half a page about the Dream Zone. The 1993 Umbra sourcebook has five pages, and provides a lot more guidance and rules. It's one reason (but not the only one) I find the 1993 version to be much superior to other editions. (One thing it includes is that each auspice has an extra, special ability they can use while in the Dream Zone or Chimares. The Galliard's power is &quot;dream shaping&quot;.) If you want to include dreams and the Dream Zone more heavily in your chronicles, I highly recommend you try to obtain a copy. I purchased my PDF online and am very glad I did.<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-07T06:45:52-08:00","id":1555202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555160#post1555160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it helps, but they not enter physically<br /> &quot;Her slumbering mind reaches through the mist of thought and into Dream itself.&quot; only their mind enter, body left behind sleeping in the Penumbra - witch is if no one guards their body is quite dangeros if not borderline suicidal<br /> I think this is quite a drawback and dangerous enough - so I let them sleep and suffer the consequences so to speak</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something I'm still debating with myself. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> mentioned:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555165#post1555165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chimares are simply domains in the Penumbra. They are linked to the Dream Zone, but the Dream Zone is separate.<br /> (..)<br /> Garou in the Penumbra may enter any Chimare they wish simply by choosing to enter them just like they do any other domain.\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>As written, there is nothing stopping Fera from entering a Chimare physically. I deliberately chose to let them enter only as dream projection for now to balance it against the Sorcerer, for whom physically entering a dream is a level 6 Path power. It is also a little more coherent (imo) and thematically appropriate, but in the end just a quirk of cross-over play.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, physically entering the Demesne of a lucid dreamer who has effectively god-like powers there is probably one of the most dangerous things you can do.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555165#post1555165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some STs do want some additional challenges when entering domains like certain dice rolls (usually involving Enigma because that is what is used to navigate the Umbra) or figuring out certain tasks or riddles. It's all up to how easy or hard you want to make it. I generally make it very easy to enter dream Chimares. Any challenges or dice rolls are what happens once they get inside and try to do something.<br /> <br /> The Galliard Gift Dreamspeak allows a Garou to enter someone's dream (a Chimare) although in this case the Garou does not need to be physically present in the Penumbra next to the Chimare to do so. Presumably when the Gift is succesfully activated, the Garou simply vanishes from their current location and appears directly into the Chimare. Although not stated in the Gift description, I assume that when the Garou wants to end it, they simply pop back out of the Chimare and return to where they originally vanished.<br /> <br /> Likewise the Galliard Gift Gift of Dreams allows Garou to craft a specific and potent dream for an individual. In essence, this creates a specific Chimare for that individual to inhabit.\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The first time a player tried to go into another's dream, I had them do a little mini-quest to establish how they would go about building a bridge between their own dream and that of the target. This is nice once as exposition, but I'm considering to formalizing it into a roll against the target Willpower for repeated instances. Enigmas is a good call on that.<br /> <br /> In terms of Gifts, I think both are fitting without intruding on the competence of the Oneiromancer too much. Rite of Dreaming + Rite of Dreamtime are pretty certain picks, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555165#post1555165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Individual dreamers do sometimes enter the Dream Zone directly from their own Chimare, but those incidents tend to be fairly rare. Certain individual people can be more prone to experience such potent, deep dreams than others.\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I think using your own Chimare as a 'springboard' to other places in the Umbra is perfectly fine, especially if it is deliberately crafted that way. If Chimares are connected to the Dream Zone, and the Dream Zone touches the rest of the Umbra, establishing a shortcut to some special spots important to the dreamer is reasonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555165#post1555165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also have a very hostile Wyrm Nightmare dreamlord reside in the Dream Zone that is actively trying to invade Gaia's dream and corrupt reality. It's basically a counterpart to Chimera and the other unnamed Dreamlords of Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div> 'Infected Dreams' is definitely something I want to play with. A dark mirror of Chimera is a really good pick for that, I was considering something Lovecraftian from outside reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555165#post1555165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Umbra sourcebooks talk about the Dream Zone, but not all sourcebooks are equal. The Revised Umbra in 2001 has half a page about the Dream Zone. The 1993 Umbra sourcebook has five pages, and provides a lot more guidance and rules. It's one reason (but not the only one) I find the 1993 version to be much superior to other editions. (One thing it includes is that each auspice has an extra, special ability they can use while in the Dream Zone or Chimares. The Galliard's power is &quot;dream shaping&quot;.) If you want to include dreams and the Dream Zone more heavily in your chronicles, I highly recommend you try to obtain a copy. I purchased my PDF online and am very glad I did.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good advice, I will have a look. I like having older editions for comparison anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T01:33:08-08:00","id":1555354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555202#post1555202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Infected Dreams' is definitely something I want to play with.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a follow-up: Has anybody played with dreams and the Dream Zone as a setting for the turf war of the Triat?<br /> <br /> While reading up on it I got the impression it's a largely autonomous realm, even the Wyld seems to be a bit more passive there. Weaver has some agents that try to extend the Pattern Web into dreams (which as written has surprisingly complicated metaphysical implications considering what the Pattern Web is, but I assume it mostly means trying to calcify the realm), and Wyrm does its usual corruption thing.<br /> <br /> Something like quasi-autonomy would be interesting to me for plot reasons, like a consciousness behind dreams that is neither Triat nor Gaian could be an interesting 'player' to add. I'm generally trying to keep away from Changeling lore (ie making the Dream Zone and the Dreaming the same thing), but I vaguely recall that being a thing there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T01:54:02-08:00","id":1555355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555354#post1555354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weaver has some agents that try to extend the Pattern Web into dreams (which as written has surprisingly complicated metaphysical implications considering what the Pattern Web is, but I assume it mostly means trying to calcify the realm), and Wyrm does its usual corruption thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the Weaver have surprisingly big influence in the Dream and the dreaming paradoxiacally in the form of the Fae - even, like Vampires, not even realizing it<br /> They are all about Laws, Order, rigid noble vs commoner system, courts , binding oaths, pledges and laws<br /> Similarly the Fomorians, the &quot;Elder Darks&quot; are could be agents of the Wyrm/Dragon of Balance/destruction, like the Murdhuacha who are the dreams of <b>Dagon</b> / Nightmare of Qyrll\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T10:08:08-08:00","id":1555362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555355#post1555355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say the Weaver have surprisingly big influence in the Dream and the dreaming paradoxiacally in the form of the Fae - even, like Vampires, not even realizing it<br /> They are all about Laws, Order, rigid noble vs commoner system, courts , binding oaths, pledges and laws\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure. True, strong hierarchic and autocratic structures are a hallmark of Weaver influence, but according to Book of the Weaver &quot;The Pattern Web is the lattice that underlies all of [...] material and Umbral reality.&quot; And the entry on Mind Spider spirits reads &quot;Mind-Spiders are dedicated to the expansion of the Pattern Web into Epiph and Dream Realms.&quot;<br /> <br /> This implies to me that Dream is independent of 'Weaver made' reality if she needs to expand the Web into there. It fits the theme, as dreams are something of a transient/virtual parallel reality. At the very least it places Dream apart from other Umbral realms, and I think the lack of Pattern Web is a sign that Weaver probably has the least influence there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T14:21:16-08:00","id":1555372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555354#post1555354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm generally trying to keep away from Changeling lore (ie making the Dream Zone and the Dreaming the same thing), but I vaguely recall that being a thing there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you're trying to keep away of the thing that can best help you further.<br /> <br /> Mostly Werewolf and Mage seemed to avoid going too much into the Dream Zone, maybe not to interfere too much with Changeling.<br /> <br /> But the reality is that the Dreaming and the Dream Zone as completely distinct entities isn't something that makes much sense. Sure, they're not completely related as the Dreaming seems to be more about creativity and stories than dreams, but the overlap is somewhat inevitable and was avoided.<br /> <br /> I don't think you should keep the Dreaming distinct from the Umbra and independent from the Dream Zone unless you actually want to run a Changeling game in the same continuity or something like that. If you just want to play WtA, then you're better off adapting it to its cosmology and pick and chose as much as you want from Changeling and discard the rest completely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T22:32:30-08:00","id":1555391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555354#post1555354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm generally trying to keep away from Changeling lore (ie making the Dream Zone and the Dreaming the same thing), but I vaguely recall that being a thing there.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that the Deep Dreaming is one of the lands of the Dream Realms, the shards of imagination. Dream Realms, also called dreamscapes, are isolated islands that dwell in a \u201csea\u201d of imaginative possibility. The Deep Dreaming is the primeval portion of the Maya. Here are massive realms called the Onerae ruled by the enigmatic Oneira, or Dream Lords. Only the comatose, mad, and the utterly fearless voyage here. Even the fae avoid this place, and the few dreamers who voyage here seldom return. Trods are the only way to travel this far. The Deep Dreaming is home to fabled Arcadia, now lost to the Changelings. Arcadia is just one of the Dream Realms of the Dream Lords. It is now cut off from Earth due to the Shattering.<br /> <br /> The Far Dreaming is essentially the Arcadia Gateway which fae call the Milderwood or Forest of Lies, and Mages call Hy-Brasil. Potent Dream realms that linger can draw dreamers again and again. Some are even communal and shared by people. Very often these communal Dream Realms are a result of popular fiction or legend, or even the cause of such stories, legends, and myths. In time such mighty Dream Realms can become mythic, and thereby permanently lodge into the Near Umbra. Arcadia Gateway is one such, presumably because the fae interact with humanity a lot.<br /> <br /> The Near Dreaming (called the Dreamtime by some such as Dreamspeakers) is the nearest contact of the Dreaming with the Realm. The Fae consider this reality their home. Why the Changeling Dreaming is so prominent of the Dream Realms (as seen by Earth's inhabitants), and the others are not is somewhat of a mystery. However, there are references to the fairy world as being part of the Dream of Gaia, overseen by her Incarna avatar Danu. This might have helped lodge the Dreaming so much closer to Earth than the other Dream Realms ruled by their own Oneira. Likewise we have references to the Incarna of Stag and Oak making mutual oaths to the fairies in the earliest days which cemented ties between our worlds. The other Dream Realms don't have this.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is not directly laid out. Bits and pieces of information are scattered throughout multiple sourcebooks, and this is mainly an artifact of second edition. The Revised era, and Changeling never got a Revised edition, liked to eliminate any ties between the game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-12T04:18:30-08:00","id":1555397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555372#post1555372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you're trying to keep away of the thing that can best help you further.<br /> <br /> Mostly Werewolf and Mage seemed to avoid going too much into the Dream Zone, maybe not to interfere too much with Changeling.<br /> <br /> But the reality is that the Dreaming and the Dream Zone as completely distinct entities isn't something that makes much sense. Sure, they're not completely related as the Dreaming seems to be more about creativity and stories than dreams, but the overlap is somewhat inevitable and was avoided.<br /> <br /> I don't think you should keep the Dreaming distinct from the Umbra and independent from the Dream Zone unless you actually want to run a Changeling game in the same continuity or something like that. If you just want to play WtA, then you're better off adapting it to its cosmology and pick and chose as much as you want from Changeling and discard the rest completely.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the plan. I'm not against taking over some elements from CtD that fit, it's just that I'm very unfamiliar with the setting and feel more comfortable with approaching it from a WtA or MtA direction.<br /> <br /> The reason why dreams as something functionally different from the rest of the Umbra is so attractive as a plot point for me is because the werespider in the group is looking for a potential replacement for Wyld, although she is unaware that is what she is doing. I ran with the Ananasi Plan B that wants to replace the current Triat with alternatives and something like a Dream Celestine could fit the bill for Wyld.. maybe. Not entirely sure yet if it actually is, but it's close enough that it's worth exploring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555391#post1555391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that the Deep Dreaming is one of the lands of the Dream Realms, the shards of imagination. Dream Realms, also called dreamscapes, are isolated islands that dwell in a \u201csea\u201d of imaginative possibility. The Deep Dreaming is the primeval portion of the Maya. Here are massive realms called the Onerae ruled by the enigmatic Oneira, or Dream Lords. Only the comatose, mad, and the utterly fearless voyage here. Even the fae avoid this place, and the few dreamers who voyage here seldom return. Trods are the only way to travel this far. The Deep Dreaming is home to fabled Arcadia, now lost to the Changelings. Arcadia is just one of the Dream Realms of the Dream Lords. It is now cut off from Earth due to the Shattering.<br /> <br /> The Far Dreaming is essentially the Arcadia Gateway which fae call the Milderwood or Forest of Lies, and Mages call Hy-Brasil. Potent Dream realms that linger can draw dreamers again and again. Some are even communal and shared by people. Very often these communal Dream Realms are a result of popular fiction or legend, or even the cause of such stories, legends, and myths. In time such mighty Dream Realms can become mythic, and thereby permanently lodge into the Near Umbra. Arcadia Gateway is one such, presumably because the fae interact with humanity a lot.<br /> <br /> The Near Dreaming (called the Dreamtime by some such as Dreamspeakers) is the nearest contact of the Dreaming with the Realm. The Fae consider this reality their home. Why the Changeling Dreaming is so prominent of the Dream Realms (as seen by Earth's inhabitants), and the others are not is somewhat of a mystery. However, there are references to the fairy world as being part of the Dream of Gaia, overseen by her Incarna avatar Danu. This might have helped lodge the Dreaming so much closer to Earth than the other Dream Realms ruled by their own Oneira. Likewise we have references to the Incarna of Stag and Oak making mutual oaths to the fairies in the earliest days which cemented ties between our worlds. The other Dream Realms don't have this.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is not directly laid out. Bits and pieces of information are scattered throughout multiple sourcebooks, and this is mainly an artifact of second edition. The Revised era, and Changeling never got a Revised edition, liked to eliminate any ties between the game lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> How would you fit the Dream Zone as described in WtA into this architecture? Something in-between the Dream Realms maybe, or just replace it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-12T06:34:15-08:00","id":1555402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555391#post1555391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, this is not directly laid out. Bits and pieces of information are scattered throughout multiple sourcebooks, and this is mainly an artifact of second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it fits perfectly for a WtA game, where Changeling lore is secondary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555397#post1555397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the plan. I'm not against taking over some elements from CtD that fit, it's just that I'm very unfamiliar with the setting and feel more comfortable with approaching it from a WtA or MtA direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll be doing so, that's not the point.<br /> <br /> Long story short, take a look at Changeling lore, either in any Core Book or the wikia, and adapt whatever fancies you. That'll give you more material to work with than you'll get asking for house rules using only WtA or MtA as basis.<br /> <br /> It's not that we can't help, but what you want <i><b>specifically</b></i> will mostly come from there anyway.<br /> <br /> Were you wanting something simpler, like a short episode in dream-logic, a few points would serve you fine. Were you wanting a more detailed set of rules, but still keeping it Umbra-as-Usual, we could easily help.<br /> <br /> But for the whole personal plot of a PC that'll end up replacing the Wyld for a Dream God? I don't think asking here is a bad take, but reading Changeling will help <u>a lot</u>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555397#post1555397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you fit the Dream Zone as described in WtA into this architecture? Something in-between the Dream Realms maybe, or just replace it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dream Zone is basically the collective of the Dream Realms, so to speak.<br /> <br /> I think the simplest way of explaining it is that passages to particular Dream Realms can be found anywhere in the Umbra (and even on Earth), but once you're in a Dream Realm they're all connected between themselves.<br /> <br /> As if the Dream Realms were bubbles scattered through the Umbra, and the Dream Zone were the 5-D foam those bubbles are actually a part of. It's less a space and more the relationship between those spaces and their collective nature. Also those bubbles are 4-D and even individually can touch unrelated places simultaneously, but most won't be that complex.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-12T07:53:47-08:00","id":1555408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555402#post1555402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll be doing so, that's not the point.<br /> <br /> Long story short, take a look at Changeling lore, either in any Core Book or the wikia, and adapt whatever fancies you. That'll give you more material to work with than you'll get asking for house rules using only WtA or MtA as basis.<br /> <br /> It's not that we can't help, but what you want <i><b>specifically</b></i> will mostly come from there anyway.<br /> <br /> Were you wanting something simpler, like a short episode in dream-logic, a few points would serve you fine. Were you wanting a more detailed set of rules, but still keeping it Umbra-as-Usual, we could easily help.<br /> <br /> But for the whole personal plot of a PC that'll end up replacing the Wyld for a Dream God? I don't think asking here is a bad take, but reading Changeling will help <u>a lot</u>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the idea was that I look at the experiences others had with dreams in WtA and build on that as I go, but perhaps that was too naive. If CtD material will help me the most, then I will look there. Do you have recommendations for resources beyond the Core Book that could help with what I'm trying to do?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555402#post1555402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dream Zone is basically the collective of the Dream Realms, so to speak.<br /> <br /> I think the simplest way of explaining it is that passages to particular Dream Realms can be found anywhere in the Umbra (and even on Earth), but once you're in a Dream Realm they're all connected between themselves.<br /> <br /> As if the Dream Realms were bubbles scattered through the Umbra, and the Dream Zone were the 5-D foam those bubbles are actually a part of. It's less a space and more the relationship between those spaces and their collective nature. Also those bubbles are 4-D and even individually can touch unrelated places simultaneously, but most won't be that complex.</div> </div> </div> </div>This already helps a lot. Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-12T13:30:57-08:00","id":1555419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555408#post1555408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have recommendations for resources beyond the Core Book that could help with what I'm trying to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>As usual C20 will get you the most out of your bang. If you have it, you have everything covered for your particular needs, the sources will be just if you want to delve deeper.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Players Guide to Changeling: The Dreaming</i></b> or <b><i>Rage Across Appalachia</i></b>- Mostly because of the <b>Nunnehi</b>, native american Kithain, as they have rules for dealing with spirits that may interest you.<br /> <br /> <b><i>The Autumn People</i></b> - Deals on all things Banality, including actual fae and half fae. It will give you an idea of how the Weaver manifests among the fae and dreams.<br /> <br /> <b><i>The Shadow Court</i></b> - Covers the Unseelie, the Thallain, and its namesake, a kind of Super Evil secret society. This will give you the Wyrm within the Dreaming, including actual ties to other supernaturals on the behalf of those fae.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Noblesse Oblige: The Book of Houses</i></b> (Seelie), <b><i>Pour L'Amour et Liberte: The Book of Houses 2</i></b> (Unseelie), and maybe <b><i>Book of Lost Houses: The Second Coming</i></b> (mostly for Scathach) - If you want to delve more into fae society without bringing it fully, I'll recommend at least some understanding of the Noble Houses, but those books are the less important here and can be substituted for the wikia no prob. Your main concerns should be <b>House Balor</b> (Unseelie) for its ties to the most Malfean-adjacent beings in Changeling, and <b>House Scathach</b> for its continued presence in the human world doing heroics and stuff when the other nobles were away.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Book of Lost Dreams</i></b> - Only if you really, really want &quot;official&quot; crossover rules. They're bad as usual, though.<br /> <br /> It's up to you which are priorities on the first three books. PGtCtD won't help you much beyond the Nunnehi, but their rules for spirits may be what you need the most, I don't know, and you can take the crash course in RAA. TAP and TSC are must haves if you want to bring the Triat through the lenses of dreams. The books of Houses you only need if you look the houses in the wikia and really want to delve deeper into them. The <i>Second Edition</i> Core Book has surface info into the Seelie Houses, so <i>Noblesse Oblige</i> is the less relevant, the others are just hinted at there. BoLD is useful only if you're having trouble with basic rules interaction, but this one I'd say you're better off asking here instead of even bothering.<br /> <br /> With C20 I would suggest to just look those things in the wikia and use the core for rules, it covers the basics on them all and updates stuff. Look for the Nunnehi, Autumn People, Thallain, the Unseelie and the Houses, that's the stuff you really need beyond the basics. You may want to look into the <b>Inanimae</b> (<b><i>Inanimae: The Secret Way</i></b>), which are Dreaming elementals, and the <b>Adhene</b> (<b><i>Denizens of the Dreaming</i></b>), which are weird fae from the Far Dreaming that may or may not be related to the Fomorians/Wyrm. But don't sweat too much over them unless you take a look and really wants to read more.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition Player's Guide</i></b> - Is the only book with really good info about the rest of the world, so if you plan to go outside the US and want to see what's there in canon, go for it. The rest of it is good, but not important for your needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T00:38:27-08:00","id":1555427,"title":"","content":"Thank you again for the detailed overview. I actually have Autumn People and used it before to import a few ideas. I think I will start with the Core and then use <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>'s cosmology overview as a jump-off point to explore specific concepts it mentioned.<br /> <br /> One more question before I dive in: the group also has a Stargazer, so I would like to involve Chimera. Does she have a role in CtD? If not, is there an entity she could substitute?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T11:43:29-08:00","id":1555431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555397#post1555397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you fit the Dream Zone as described in WtA into this architecture? Something in-between the Dream Realms maybe, or just replace it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dream Zone, as its name suggests, is a Zone which is an umbral term of art. A Zone is an independent reality that is an inherent part of the Umbra, but which is hard to define or explain. (The other two known Zones are the Mirror Zone and Null Zone, but more are thought to exist.) No matter how much Garou or mages known about Zones, there is a mystery about them. They defy rational thought and categorization. Zones are separate from other aspects of the Umbra, but also connected to them. So the Dream Zone, directly connected to the material world by the dreams of its inhabitants (Chimares) is also an incredibly distant and exotic part of the Umbra.<br /> <br /> A general description of the dream realms, and the geography of the Dreaming, can be found in the Book of Worlds for Mage: the Ascension (page 79). So the Dream Realms are beyond the Far Dreaming (aka the Arcadia Gateway in the Near Umbra). Where the Horizon (or Membrane as the Garou call it) bisects the Dreaming, on the other side is the Deep Dreaming (where the Oneiri or Dreamlords dwell).<br /> <br /> So the Dreaming of the Changelings is technically part of the Dream Zone, but the Dream Zone is much, much more than that. Most Garou probably don't connect the two together at all since they are more familiar with Changeling Freeholds (because they can become caerns and also entrances to the Near Dreaming), Trods (the Penumbral domains that connect to the Near Dreaming which Changelings call the Green Paths of Balor), and the Arcadia Gateway (which is the Far Dreaming). Those are much easier connections for them than trying to reach the fairy world in a long runabout way through the Dream Zone. In my games, I have almost every Stag pack totem just know how to enter the fairy realms through well known Trods if their packs ever want to go through them and encounter the fairy world.<br /> <br /> When Garou want to undergo spirit quests to the Dream Zone its because of actual dreams of people. That it is somehow connected to the fairy world is just one of those mysterious things that don't make sense which is why the Dream Zone is classified as a Zone.<br /> <br /> Likewise the Dream Zone also connects to the Dark Umbra because wraiths with the Phantasm Arcanoi also interact with dreams and can create entire special Dream Theatres that take place in the Dream Zone (but they're also part of the Dark Umbra). The Dream Zone in fact links to lots of different places, and there seems to be more than one mention of a link to the Black Labyrinth of Malfeas. But we normally don't think of those places as &quot;part&quot; of the Dream Zone.<br /> <br /> The Dream Zone is just a very weird place.<br /> <br /> When I was compiling my own handbook on running scenes/encounters for dreams, the sourcebooks I pulled from were Umbra: the Velvet Shadow from WtA, Book of Worlds from MtA, Dreams and Nightmares from CtD, and Guildbook: Sandmen from WtA. The first two had the most important information with the latter two only really being used for completion's sake since dreams can link to those two settings. The Book of Worlds also give descriptions of some of the other Dream Realms that exist, but of course there cannot be an exhaustive list of such realms, nor any idea of how &quot;big&quot; or &quot;important&quot; each one is relative to one another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T16:58:22-08:00","id":1555444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555427#post1555427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One more question before I dive in: the group also has a Stargazer, so I would like to involve Chimera. Does she have a role in CtD? If not, is there an entity she could substitute?</div> </div> </div> </div>No role, but nothing barring it,either.<br /> <br /> CtD doesn't usually deal with this kind of entity, but they totally can exist out there. For most Changelings it wouldn't be distinguishable in the Dreaming from any other Chimera (in their terms, a dream-thing that isn't part of a regular enough structure to be a fae). They don't have gods or something, and they accept the nature of the Dreaming without ever questioning if there's something actually guiding it in any way, shape or form, they accept its (mostly narrative) logic at face value.<br /> <br /> So the totem may have any role whatsoever you want, and probably only those who deal with spirits will be able to notice. But at the same time, since you want this to be a place that surprises your players in how it works differently from the Umbra at large, limiting Chimera's power over the place may be a good idea. It may still be vastly knowable, and able to help in many ways, just not in the ways the PCs expect.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that a few Changelings, like the Nunnehi, deal with spirits and even have totems. But they deal with spirits through normal Umbra, as a somewhat distinct thing.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>'s cosmology on both posts is the state-of-the-art you'll find on the WtA part of the equation, as he already knows a lot about the rest of the WoD, but tackles this from the WtA perspective. Changeling will help you big with the part on making it different and surprising, and maybe adding fae NPCs if you feel it will be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T05:59:05-08:00","id":1555472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555444#post1555444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the totem may have any role whatsoever you want, and probably only those who deal with spirits will be able to notice. But at the same time, since you want this to be a place that surprises your players in how it works differently from the Umbra at large, limiting Chimera's power over the place may be a good idea. It may still be vastly knowable, and able to help in many ways, just not in the ways the PCs expect.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that a few Changelings, like the Nunnehi, deal with spirits and even have totems. But they deal with spirits through normal Umbra, as a somewhat distinct thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I will probably use her mainly in the role of guide and handwave her motivation for now unless I stumble on something that is a good fit. Some editions describe her as a totem of dreams, others of enigmas, and I have been using both aspects for her. Not a big problem if her goals are inscrutable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555431#post1555431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise the Dream Zone also connects to the Dark Umbra because wraiths with the Phantasm Arcanoi also interact with dreams and can create entire special Dream Theatres that take place in the Dream Zone (but they're also part of the Dark Umbra). The Dream Zone in fact links to lots of different places, and there seems to be more than one mention of a link to the Black Labyrinth of Malfeas. But we normally don't think of those places as &quot;part&quot; of the Dream Zone.<br /> <br /> The Dream Zone is just a very weird place.<br /> <br /> When I was compiling my own handbook on running scenes/encounters for dreams, the sourcebooks I pulled from were Umbra: the Velvet Shadow from WtA, Book of Worlds from MtA, Dreams and Nightmares from CtD, and Guildbook: Sandmen from WtA. The first two had the most important information with the latter two only really being used for completion's sake since dreams can link to those two settings. The Book of Worlds also give descriptions of some of the other Dream Realms that exist, but of course there cannot be an exhaustive list of such realms, nor any idea of how &quot;big&quot; or &quot;important&quot; each one is relative to one another.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have already planned to have one leg of the journey be the underworld and adjacent dream space, the link between memory and dreams is too intriguing to not make use of. Since even Wraiths in Slumber can sometimes dream, it opens up some great opportunities to explore the history of an artifact/Fetter as lead-in. But I think I will take that to the WtO forums once I have specific questions.<br /> <br /> Thank you again both for your answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-26T04:37:34-08:00","id":1555884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555391#post1555391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Deep Dreaming is the primeval portion of the Maya. Here are massive realms called the Onerae ruled by the enigmatic Oneira, or Dream Lords.</div> </div> </div> </div>I need to sort out my thoughts on the Oneira a bit, since I'm still conceptualizing the general metaphysics. Any help or thoughts on that are very welcome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreams and Nightmares</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Within the flood of echoes that is the Deep Dreaming, the eleven crystalline realms of the Oneiroi whirl and ring, churning the stuff of Dreams in their wake. One of these realms was once known as Arcadia; now, it is sealed from within, and any who depart from it can never return. As for the other Oneiric Realms, those of Moros and Hemera, Aether and Ker, Hypnates and D\u00e1n, Charis and Momus, Dik\u00e9 and Protea, little is known.</div> </div> </div> </div>So these are (mostly) modeled after the Theogony's children of Nyx and even uses the proper Oreinoi moniker, with some liberties:<br /> <br /> Moros - the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moros\" target=\"_blank\">same</a><br /> Hemera - the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hemera\" target=\"_blank\">same</a><br /> Aether - the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aether_(mythology)\" target=\"_blank\">same</a><br /> Ker - the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keres\" target=\"_blank\">same</a><br /> Hypnates - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypnos\" target=\"_blank\">Hypnos</a><br /> D\u00e1n - the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moirai\" target=\"_blank\">Moirai</a>, as per description<br /> Charis - the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charites\" target=\"_blank\">Graces</a><br /> Momus - the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Momus\" target=\"_blank\">same</a><br /> Dik\u00e9 - the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dike_(mythology)\" target=\"_blank\">same</a><br /> Protea - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proteus\" target=\"_blank\">Proteus </a>or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morpheus\" target=\"_blank\">Morpheus </a>(if the Morphean Oracles of House Scathach are an indicator)<br /> <br /> Beyond those are Night (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nyx\" target=\"_blank\">Nyx</a>) and Silence (possibly <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harpocrates\" target=\"_blank\">Horus</a>?).<br /> <br /> This fits with the assessment in <i>Book of Worlds</i> that the Oneira are archetypes that fuel the lower reaches of dreams with their concepts, I see them in a similar role Incarna for spirits would take.<br /> The question mark here is of course Arcadia - there are plenty of Nyx' children left, but unless I missed an explicit mention somewhere, the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arcadia_(utopia)\" target=\"_blank\">utopia version</a> seems to actually fit the Gaian Dream.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dream and Nightmares</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beyond Silence, at the deepest possible realm of the Dreaming, the world opens up upon itself and darkness becomes transmuted into wonder.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we follow the Theogony, this would be <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chaos_(cosmogony)\" target=\"_blank\">Chaos</a>, ie the Wyld, which as the deepest source of dreams makes sense.<br /> <br /> From this description I would assume that the Oneira serve as a mechanism to shape the raw chaos into fundamental archetypes, and from there it further diversifies through the hierarchy of Fae. The interesting thing is that this is a Weaver function, and some of the things that went wrong in the Dreaming might be the result of her going insane after being bound.<br /> <br /> Anyways, because I'm putting on my WtA goggles while looking at this, I may be as well be completely off the mark. If so, please let me know.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-26T12:12:17-08:00","id":1555888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555884#post1555884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need to sort out my thoughts on the Oneira a bit, since I'm still conceptualizing the general metaphysics. Any help or thoughts on that are very welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Oneira aren't developed by the original sourcebooks. The most information we have is about Chimera whom the Garou consider the greatest of the Dream Lords (because She of Many Faces is one of their totems). I believe we only get one other Oneiri's name in a published sourcebook, Myathia of the Twelve Collars who is name dropped in Book of Worlds for Mage. No other information is revealed about her that I can find.<br /> <br /> Guildbook: Sandman also contains a legend concerning a being called Somnus. Somnus is mentioned with various other beings that are clear counterparts to the Endless in Neil Gaiman's Sandman comic book series. Like much of White Wolf's work, these beings are given a combination of both Latin and Greek names. Since Somnus is obviously a Dream/Morpheus type figure, you could easily use that name for another Oneiri.<br /> <br /> Truthfully, in my own conceptions of the Oneiri and their role in the Dream Zone, I steal as much as I can from Gaiman's Sandman comic books. It's an easy source of inspiration, and I figure it's probably what most people would want in any scene involving the Oneiri specifically or the Dream Zone in general.<br /> <br /> In my chronicles, &quot;Somnus&quot; is my version of Morpheus and is the main Dream Lord of humanity. Chimera serves the same function for the Changing Breeds, but also has the portfolio of Enigmas and mysteries.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I try to figure out what other aspects of dreaming I would want to distinguish from one another. Much like how Chimera personifies engimas, and thus engimatic dreams that one has to figure out what they mean for self-infight or prophecy. An obvious one would be fears and nightmares. Nightmare lord figures can be found in lots of media. Erotic dreams could also be a good distinguisher. It all depends on what you might think is a good distinguisher if you want to use multiple Dreamlords instead of just defaulting most dreams to just one.<br /> <br /> I've sometimes considered whether to make the aforementioned Myathia of the Twelve Collars the Dreamlord of the dreams of animals.<br /> <br /> I also think a dreamlord of some kind of Dunsanian/Lovecraftian fantasy Dreamlands that is its own &quot;reality&quot; that some dreamers could visit may be nice. We've already been told of the mythic dream city of Syrannon in WoD: Sorcerer which I've taken to meant to be similar to the Dreamlands, and there are some very good Dreamlands sourcebooks already put out for the Call of Cthulhu RPG (there's also an intriguing <a href=\"https://www.dreamrpg.com/\" target=\"_blank\">upcoming RPG</a> based on that from the artist Jason Bradley Thompson). So lots of easy inspiration for somebody who wanted to develop their own WoD version of that. I think that would be sufficiently different from most dreams and dreamlords, since the lord of the Dreamlands is basically a variant of Nyarlathotep.<br /> <br /> And as I previously mentioned, I also have an &quot;invading&quot; alien Dreamlord trying to reach Earth's Dream Zone so that there is a Wyrm counterpart to Chimera, and to give something for Stargazers and packs under Chimera to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T13:50:42-08:00","id":1555920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555888#post1555888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Oneira aren't developed by the original sourcebooks. The most information we have is about Chimera whom the Garou consider the greatest of the Dream Lords (because She of Many Faces is one of their totems). I believe we only get one other Oneiri's name in a published sourcebook, Myathia of the Twelve Collars who is name dropped in Book of Worlds for Mage. No other information is revealed about her that I can find.<br /> <br /> Guildbook: Sandman also contains a legend concerning a being called Somnus. Somnus is mentioned with various other beings that are clear counterparts to the Endless in Neil Gaiman's Sandman comic book series. Like much of White Wolf's work, these beings are given a combination of both Latin and Greek names. Since Somnus is obviously a Dream/Morpheus type figure, you could easily use that name for another Oneiri.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it seems that they largely left them for the ST as a 'fill-in' option, and I will adjust them to what I need. To be honest, I don't know if the players are ever going to go that deep, so it is mostly for myself to have a basis to build upon. The Theogony as a rough framework for orientation works well enough, the specifics maybe don't matter as much. That said, having Chimera as one of the actual Dream Lords is an interesting option; at that level the difference between Dream and Spirit are largely semantic, and it would be a nice element to include for one of my players.<br /> <br /> As an aside here, I liked the parallel between the Silver Sea at the threshold of the Deep Dreaming and the Tempest of the Underworld. There is some interesting potential to connect these two via the Dream Zone and the concept of Memory that is shared between them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555888#post1555888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Truthfully, in my own conceptions of the Oneiri and their role in the Dream Zone, I steal as much as I can from Gaiman's Sandman comic books. It's an easy source of inspiration, and I figure it's probably what most people would want in any scene involving the Oneiri specifically or the Dream Zone in general.<br /> <br /> In my chronicles, &quot;Somnus&quot; is my version of Morpheus and is the main Dream Lord of humanity. Chimera serves the same function for the Changing Breeds, but also has the portfolio of Enigmas and mysteries.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I try to figure out what other aspects of dreaming I would want to distinguish from one another. Much like how Chimera personifies engimas, and thus engimatic dreams that one has to figure out what they mean for self-infight or prophecy. An obvious one would be fears and nightmares. Nightmare lord figures can be found in lots of media. Erotic dreams could also be a good distinguisher. It all depends on what you might think is a good distinguisher if you want to use multiple Dreamlords instead of just defaulting most dreams to just one.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Using the Endless from Sandman as a template would be the intuitive thing for me, too. However, I think for the chronicle I'm running specifically, I will modify their concept a little. Since the focus is on the triatic influence on different realms (and Weaver influence in particular), my current sketch for the functional structure is like this:<br /> <br /> <b>Wyld</b><br /> Raw Chaos / Negentropy<br /> <b>\u2193</b><br /> <b>Silence / Erebus</b><br /> Functions as a filter and refines the raw chaos<br /> Wyrm function. Used to discard 'less pure' bits but lets more of them through now.<br /> <b>\u2193</b><br /> <b>Night / Nyx</b><br /> Transmutes the refined chaos into raw Dream Stuff<br /> Weaver function. Still mostly working as intended, but disoriented.<br /> <b>\u2193</b><br /> <b>Oneiroi</b><br /> \u200bAdd archetype attributes to the Dream Stuff: Love, Mystery, Fate, Hope, etc.<br /> <br /> If I want a central figure like the Endless version of Morpheus, the Night / Nyx tier would be where I put it - the shaper / weaver.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555888#post1555888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think a dreamlord of some kind of Dunsanian/Lovecraftian fantasy Dreamlands that is its own &quot;reality&quot; that some dreamers could visit may be nice. We've already been told of the mythic dream city of Syrannon in WoD: Sorcerer which I've taken to meant to be similar to the Dreamlands, and there are some very good Dreamlands sourcebooks already put out for the Call of Cthulhu RPG (there's also an intriguing <a href=\"https://www.dreamrpg.com/\" target=\"_blank\">upcoming RPG</a> based on that from the artist Jason Bradley Thompson). So lots of easy inspiration for somebody who wanted to develop their own WoD version of that. I think that would be sufficiently different from most dreams and dreamlords, since the lord of the Dreamlands is basically a variant of Nyarlathotep.<br /> <br /> And as I previously mentioned, I also have an &quot;invading&quot; alien Dreamlord trying to reach Earth's Dream Zone so that there is a Wyrm counterpart to Chimera, and to give something for Stargazers and packs under Chimera to do.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>As is, the whimsy (I hope that is the right English word; it's not meant negatively) of the CtD setting would clash somewhat fiercely with the tone of the campaign so far, and moving the presentation more towards a Lovecraftian experience in general might be a solution to that. Maybe the malfunctioning pair of Silence and Night has begun to let raw material from an 'outside source' through - I consider nightmares and bad dreams part of the normal state of affairs, so having cosmic horror as an alternative for 'taint' is a good option. A high level source like a Neverborn (which could further connect Underworld and Dreaming) poisoning Wyld's input or something along those lines.<br /> <br /> Thank you for the input, that kicked off some good lines of ideas to follow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T16:47:26-08:00","id":1555963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555920#post1555920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As is, the whimsy (I hope that is the right English word; it's not meant negatively) of the CtD setting would clash somewhat fiercely with the tone of the campaign so far, and moving the presentation more towards a Lovecraftian experience in general might be a solution to that. Maybe the malfunctioning pair of Silence and Night has begun to let raw material from an 'outside source' through - I consider nightmares and bad dreams part of the normal state of affairs, so having cosmic horror as an alternative for 'taint' is a good option. A high level source like a Neverborn (which could further connect Underworld and Dreaming) poisoning Wyld's input or something along those lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is the correct word, it isn't inherently negative or anything.<br /> <br /> But I want to raise a few points here: first, Lovecraft's <i>Dream Cycle</i> and his <i>Dreamlands</i> are quite whimsical on their own. While you'll see a number of horror things, it's not your regular cosmic horror. Which brings the second, you can't actually take whimsy out of dreams. That's a lot of what gives them their weirdness, as they refuse to work under &quot;rational&quot; or &quot;natural&quot; rules.<br /> <br /> Third and tying to the other two, a lot of people don't get what Changeling's whimsy is (or at least can be), and how it can be used in non-whimsical plots.<br /> <br /> Working with dreams in a &quot;serious&quot; game will probably focus on shock, contradiction, weirdness and contrast. Shock comes from how quickly dreams evolve into nightmares and how extreme they can be. This is not necessarily <i>Alice in Wonderland</i>, it can as easily be <i>It</i>, <i>Call of Cthulhu</i> or <i>Nightmare in Elm Street</i>, or even simply a Slasher movie. The Joker is as valid a dream entity as anything else, and fae can be as violent and gore as any Werewolf, but with far less reason.<br /> <br /> Contrast comes from how apparent whimsy can reveal horror or terror without an actual change. Make-up made with human fluids, fancy furniture with internal organs begging for mercy, a laughing clown that helps the Pack while snacking on living children that may well be, indeed, living children from the Waking World. Or any situation that while it resembles a game or something like that, is as serious as it gets for either tragedy or horror.<br /> <br /> All over the place in a dream there's weirdness, things that don't follow the logic PCs expect. They do follow <i>some</i> logic, though, the point is for you to define what this logic is. In this sense, the Umbra can be thought as one kind of dream-logic, as many things resemble the material world in some way, but they don't work as in the material, so for a newcomer they make no sense until they learn how spirits work. The difference with dreams is that the logic of one isn't necessarily the logic of another. You can design a logic based on the mental state of a dreamer, or a story genre, or a word-game, whatever you want for that particular dream.<br /> <br /> Finally, you can use the more benevolent aspects of dreams to contrast with more serious stuff to have your PCs know what's at stake. I personally find horror and drama too bland when it's pure cynicism, grimdark with nothing to contrast the darkness, and it's definitely not what Werewolf is built upon. In this sense the dreams are just another aspect of nature. Whimsy is also a version of idyllic, which is the main contrast of Werewolf. It's nature as it pertains to dreams when things are balanced and corruption is held at bay. It doesn't have to be extreme or all over the place, just be there enough for the PCs to know what is being lost as the world tumbles towards the Apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T06:02:04-08:00","id":1555973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555963#post1555963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I want to raise a few points here: first, Lovecraft's <i>Dream Cycle</i> and his <i>Dreamlands</i> are quite whimsical on their own. While you'll see a number of horror things, it's not your regular cosmic horror. Which brings the second, you can't actually take whimsy out of dreams. That's a lot of what gives them their weirdness, as they refuse to work under &quot;rational&quot; or &quot;natural&quot; rules.<br /> <br /> Third and tying to the other two, a lot of people don't get what Changeling's whimsy is (or at least can be), and how it can be used in non-whimsical plots.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least in my case this was influenced by how the books present the setting, although it is also apparent one can vary the presentation to something that is better suited to personal preference. I don't see it as a binary thing either; I don't need to (and neither should I) eliminate whimsy in order to adapt it. Adjusting it should work just fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555963#post1555963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Working with dreams in a &quot;serious&quot; game will probably focus on shock, contradiction, weirdness and contrast. Shock comes from how quickly dreams evolve into nightmares and how extreme they can be. This is not necessarily <i>Alice in Wonderland</i>, it can as easily be <i>It</i>, <i>Call of Cthulhu</i> or <i>Nightmare in Elm Street</i>, or even simply a Slasher movie. The Joker is as valid a dream entity as anything else, and fae can be as violent and gore as any Werewolf, but with far less reason.<br /> <br /> Contrast comes from how apparent whimsy can reveal horror or terror without an actual change. Make-up made with human fluids, fancy furniture with internal organs begging for mercy, a laughing clown that helps the Pack while snacking on living children that may well be, indeed, living children from the Waking World. Or any situation that while it resembles a game or something like that, is as serious as it gets for either tragedy or horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree - it again comes down to how the whimsical elements are presented. What I'm doing at the moment is to decide which elements are useful to adapt for the presentation I think would fit with the campaign, and which are not. For example, I think many of the pseudo-medieval, high fantasy elements would be an ill fit thematically, so I'm going to skip them in favor of something more <i>Shadowrun</i> (vaguely, probably a lot more solarpunk and much less cyberware). I think what I'm trying to say is that I'm changing the flavor of whimsy, rather than removing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555963#post1555963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All over the place in a dream there's weirdness, things that don't follow the logic PCs expect. They do follow <i>some</i> logic, though, the point is for you to define what this logic is. In this sense, the Umbra can be thought as one kind of dream-logic, as many things resemble the material world in some way, but they don't work as in the material, so for a newcomer they make no sense until they learn how spirits work. The difference with dreams is that the logic of one isn't necessarily the logic of another. You can design a logic based on the mental state of a dreamer, or a story genre, or a word-game, whatever you want for that particular dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far I have oriented myself a lot on David Lynch when it came to the narrative flow of presenting dreams. Absurdity is probably the most useful element to differentiate the experience of dreams to umbral realms, which (usually) follow a stricter logic dependent on their themes. I'm also drawing a lot on 1920s German expressionist cinema, although I'm reserving the visual representation in those for the Underworld. Crossover play certainly introduces some difficulties in deciding which concepts fuse and which do not - the functional difference between umbral realms and dreams can be paper thin at times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555963#post1555963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, you can use the more benevolent aspects of dreams to contrast with more serious stuff to have your PCs know what's at stake. I personally find horror and drama too bland when it's pure cynicism, grimdark with nothing to contrast the darkness, and it's definitely not what Werewolf is built upon. In this sense the dreams are just another aspect of nature. Whimsy is also a version of idyllic, which is the main contrast of Werewolf. It's nature as it pertains to dreams when things are balanced and corruption is held at bay. It doesn't have to be extreme or all over the place, just be there enough for the PCs to know what is being lost as the world tumbles towards the Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Dreams are intrinsically tied to hope, and in my opinion hope is - despite and because of the stark contrast to the grimdark of the setting - a theme so central to WtA that without it, it would not work.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T22:28:17-08:00","id":1556084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555920#post1555920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I consider nightmares and bad dreams part of the normal state of affairs, so having cosmic horror as an alternative for 'taint' is a good option.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that &quot;nightmare&quot; by itself is a neutral concept. A Dreamlord of Nightmare could still be an antagonist, but doesn't need to be of the Wyrm. I think the &quot;main&quot; nightmare spirits are Phantasms, and their description says they feed off malignant energy from dreams. They help dreamers relieve stress by unlocking their negative emotions. They actually protect the Dream Zone against the Triat, which is an interesting concept as it places the Dream Zone as something unique and different from standard Garou cosmology of the &quot;real world&quot;.<br /> <br /> Phantasms, like some other dream spirits, are only mentioned in the first edition Umbra sourcebook. It's another reason why I like it so much than other versions.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are other types of dream and nightmare spirits, including actual Banes. But nightmares, in and of themselves, are not inherently &quot;bad&quot; or &quot;evil&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555920#post1555920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A high level source like a Neverborn (which could further connect Underworld and Dreaming) poisoning Wyld's input or something along those lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wraith definitely deals with a lot of issues regarding the subconscious and metaphysics of the World of the Darkness, so connecting them in some ways to dreams is just natural. I leave my particular &quot;invading&quot; Dreamlord to be something alien and utterly enigmatic, but there's no reason it can't be connected to some Neverborn. After all, they are &quot;sleeping&quot; and dreaming a lot (all?) of the more active greater evils of the WoD.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T12:25:34-08:00","id":1556099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1556084#post1556084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that &quot;nightmare&quot; by itself is a neutral concept. A Dreamlord of Nightmare could still be an antagonist, but doesn't need to be of the Wyrm. I think the &quot;main&quot; nightmare spirits are Phantasms, and their description says they feed off malignant energy from dreams. They help dreamers relieve stress by unlocking their negative emotions. They actually protect the Dream Zone against the Triat, which is an interesting concept as it places the Dream Zone as something unique and different from standard Garou cosmology of the &quot;real world&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>For whatever it's worth, while not addressing the Triat directly, Changeling has most forms of Nightmare being normal dream folk. Redcaps are mostly nightmares, as are most members of the Unseelie Court (or any Changeling under their Unseelie Legacy). There are a few nightmares that are noted as exceptional, though.<br /> <br /> The Fomorians (that may or may not be connected to fomors) are lovecraftian nightmares from the &quot;Time Before Time&quot;, the Shadow Court has serious Wyrm vibes to it. Thallain seem to be Kithain Changelings &quot;fallen&quot; to a forever-Unseelie state that looks a lot like Wyrm corruption. The Dark-Kin are the only batch of extra-core nightmare fae that don't seem to be linked to anything lovecraftian or Wyrmish, just residents of the Dreaming that never dwelled for long in the Material and don't follow the Changeling Way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T12:33:28-08:00","id":1556100,"title":"","content":"Just for the sake of clarification: the word Fomorian comes from Irish Mythology, so its presence in Changeling was a given regardless of its use in WtA as Changeling basically assumes Irish Mythology as its foundational mythos the same way Vampire does the Bible.<br /> <br /> Any relationship between them and Wyrm fomors is up in the air, really. Is this just a coincidence? Are they completely distinct things whose names inspired the other or where both inspired by the same third thing? Are fomors not completely what Garou think, but manifestations of those nightmare ancients? Are those ancients old and exceedingly powerful fomors?<br /> <br /> Well, given how much Garou spiel takes freely from a lot of unrelated sources, it's fairly probable that Garou just heard and adopted the word, as it was indeed what actually happened IRL, but the other options may make for interesting plot points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T14:27:01-08:00","id":1556104,"title":"","content":"I think there were implications that the Fianna had culture cache as the &quot;bard tribe&quot;, so their take on things became the lingua lupa of the Garou Nation. And since that was one of the places that they grew up, bam, Watsonian explanation for the consequences of the Doylist &quot;I was reading Irish folklore at the time and decided to throw it in.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T15:42:29-08:00","id":1556106,"title":"","content":"I'm currently collecting ingredients for making the story, and Fomorians are an option to tie in the 'outside influence'. I don't really think they are more than superficially connected to fomors, the WOD has too long of a record of slapping cool sounding names on totally different concepts. They strike me more as what the titans were to the gods in Greek mythology.<br /> <br /> Denizens will probably make up the most common encounters, as their distance to the waking world makes them more suited for a surreal mood. There are the Keremet which I like in concept, but am not sure about the execution. Did they ever get mentioned in WtO?<br /> <br /> There's also &quot;Nightmare avatar of the Impergium&quot; in my notes, but that's probably going to fall under the cutting table. I mean, the collective subconsciousness of humanity still remembers the horrors well enough to induce Delirium, so it's probably a thing. But it's a bit too on the nose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1556084#post1556084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wraith definitely deals with a lot of issues regarding the subconscious and metaphysics of the World of the Darkness, so connecting them in some ways to dreams is just natural.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm so intrigued by this. On revisiting the Sandmen source book, Phantasm might just be the most overpowered Arcanos: escapism, dream (umbral) travel, dig up memories from dreams (Relics?), divination through oracular dreams, manipulate emotions, manipulate Shadow/Psyche balance... not to mention all the fun metaphysical questions. But yeah, that's probably better to put into the WtO forums at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T16:39:02-08:00","id":1556108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1556106#post1556106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently collecting ingredients for making the story, and Fomorians are an option to tie in the 'outside influence'. I don't really think they are more than superficially connected to fomors, the WOD has too long of a record of slapping cool sounding names on totally different concepts. They strike me more as what the titans were to the gods in Greek mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fomors are definitely just a cool word slapped at a vaguely similar thing, those are just ideas if you feel like doing it. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Saur Ops Specialist</a>'s explanation is by far the simplest and most probable if you ever need one.<br /> <br /> Conceptually the Changeling version is something like the Titans, or rather a popular modern use of the Titans, especially when compared to CtD's Tuatha. They have a lot of Lovecraftian vibes that you can either ramp up if you want Cosmic Horror, or actually tone down to make a &quot;Nature Horror&quot; theme that's very fitting to Werewolf: they're the nightmares of survival in a world before civilization, either the nightmares of humanity before it was distinct from other animals or something even older, nightmares from before humanity at all.<br /> <br /> They may be, then, a glimpse over the Dream Realms before the Madness of the Weaver, even if you decide they're only a part of it or currently tainted by the Wyrm. And Garou may be in a better position to understand them than the Changelings and other modern fae, who are intrinsically tied to civilization and the dreams that come with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1556106#post1556106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Denizens will probably make up the most common encounters, as their distance to the waking world makes them more suited for a surreal mood. There are the Keremet which I like in concept, but am not sure about the execution. Did they ever get mentioned in WtO?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure, but I don't think so.<br /> <br /> Personally I've been toying with expanding the rules on Denizens to other fae as a means to explore what the Kithain were before the Changeling Way, and how some of them may even still be. I think they're simple enough to attach to Changelings, and you may use that to adapt other Kiths and stuff to the Denizen feel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1556106#post1556106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also &quot;Nightmare avatar of the Impergium&quot; in my notes, but that's probably going to fall under the cutting table. I mean, the collective subconsciousness of humanity still remembers the horrors well enough to induce Delirium, so it's probably a thing. But it's a bit too on the nose.</div> </div> </div> </div>A realm about it would be better than a single entity. Dreams are less centered in a figure like a Lord and more in how the whole fabric of reality is defined by a theme or idea.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I think the Redcaps could already be related to that in some way? They may well be remnants of the impacts of the <i>Impergium</i> as dreams of wanton destruction through primal consumption.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}